  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN220.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟi vantu nīṅkun talaimakaṉai yetirppaṭṭut tōḻi colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said when encountering HIM who was leaving after having come to the night tryst.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN220.1">
        <l>ūruñ cēriyu muṭaṉiyain talareḻat</l>
        <l><supplied>tēro</supplied>ṭu maṟu<supplied>ki</supplied>yum paṇimoḻi payiṟṟiyuṅ</l>
        <l>keṭāat tīyi ṉurukeḻuc cellūrk</l>
        <l>kaṭāa yāṉaik kuḻūuccaman tataiya</l>
        <l>maṉmaruṅ kaṟutta maḻuvā ṇeṭiyōṉ</l>
        <l>muṉmuyaṉ ṟaritaṉiṉ muṭitta vēḷvik</l>
        <l>kayiṟarai yātta kāṇṭaku vaṉappi</l>
        <l>ṉaruṅkaṭi neṭuntūṇ pōla yāvaruṅ</l>
        <l>kāṇa lākā māṇe<supplied>ḻi</supplied> lāka</l>
        <l>muḷḷutoṟum paṉikku neñciṉai nīyē</l>
        <l>neṭumpuṟa nilaiyiṉai varuntiṉai yāyiṉ</l>
        <l>muḻaṅkukaṭa lōtaṅ kālaik koṭkum</l>
        <l>paḻampaṉ ṉelli ṉūṉū rāṅka</l>
        <l>ṇōlā virumpuṭ pōla neñcamarntu</l>
        <l>kātaṉ māṟāk kāmar puṇarcciyi</l>
        <l>ṉiruṅkaḻi mukanta ceṅkō lavvalai</l>
        <l><supplied>mu</supplied>ṭaṅkupu<supplied>ṟa</supplied> viṟavō ṭiṉamīṉ ceṟikku</l>
        <l>neṭuṅkatirk kaḻaṉit taṇcāayk kāṉat</l>
        <l>tiyāṇart taṇpaṇai yuṟumeṉa kāṉa</l>
        <l>lāya māynta cāyiṟaip paṇaittō</l>
        <l>ṇalleḻil citaiyā vēmañ</l>
        <l>colliṉit teyyayān teḷiyu māṟē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2">Having whirled along with [your] chariot and repeated humble words</l>
        <l corresp="1">so that gossip arose equally in the village and in the quarter,</l>
        <l corresp="10">o you with a heart that trembles each time you remember</l>
        <l corresp="9">[her] glorious [and] graceful bosom, not to be seen</l>
        <l corresp="8">by anyone, like the heavily protected tall pillar,</l>
        <l corresp="7">of a beauty fit to be seen, to the bottom of which a rope is tied</l>
        <l corresp="6">for the sacrifice that was completed with difficulty(?), making an effort in front</l>
        <l corresp="5">of the tall one with an axe for a weapon, who cut open the side of kings,</l>
        <l corresp="4">when the battle was packed with a crowd of rutting elephants,</l>
        <l corresp="3">in awe-inspiring Cellūr with [its] unextinguished fire(?),</l>
        <l corresp="11">- in case you should suffer from standing outside for a long [time],</l>
        <l corresp="22">speak now, in a way that we understand,</l>
        <l corresp="21">of protection, so that the good grace is not wasted</l>
        <l corresp="20">in [her] bamboo shoulders with flexible joints, chosen among the companions</l>
        <l corresp="19">in the seashore grove, [with the words]: “it resembles the fertile cool bamboo</l>
        <l corresp="18">of cool Cāaykkāṉam, [surrounded by] fields with long ears,</l>
        <l corresp="16">where the pretty nets with straight rods that are drawn from the dark backwaters</l>
        <l corresp="17">tighten over various fish together with hunch-backed prawn”,</l>
        <l corresp="15">[not wasted] in [this] passionate union, love unchanging,</l>
        <l corresp="14">hearts remaining like big birds that cannot endure(?),</l>
        <l corresp="13">there in Ūṉūr of old with much rice,</l>
        <l corresp="12">where time revolves with the flood of the thundering sea.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

